      en: ["Elevation: 7,861 meters (25,791 feet) above sea level", "Location: Khumbu region, part of the Everest massif", "First Ascent: May 16, 1961, by a British-Nepalese team", "Name meaning: \"West Peak\" in Tibetan", "Ridge: Comprises seven distinct summits", "Climbing: Known for the extreme difficulty of its massive South Face"],
